[# design_decision.j2 — DECISION block: options table + chosen + rationale.

   Adapted from a real refactor PR pattern. Table column shape is your call —
   common: {option, pro, con} or {option, complexity, perf, risk}.

   Variables expected in scope:
     decision_title:    short heading (e.g. 'Cache invalidation strategy')
     decision_options:  array of objects — first row's keys become columns
     chosen:            short label of the chosen option (e.g. 'B. Synchronous join')
     rationale:         one-line justification

   Inline form:
     ### Decision: Cache invalidation strategy

     | option | pro | con |
     | :--- | :--- | :--- |
     | A. Materialized view | cheap reads | stale until refresh |
     | B. Synchronous join | fresh reads | 8x wall cost |

     **Chosen:** A. Materialized view

     **Rationale:** staleness budget (15min) is acceptable per product spec.
